Description: Querencia Desktop file manager (beta)
 Querencia Dateien is the file manager of Querencia Desktop, a classic
 desktop in the style of GNOME 2. It follows the browser mode of
 Nautilus 2.30: menu bar, toolbar, path bar, side pane with places and
 bookmarks, tabs, icon, list and compact view and a status bar. Files are
 copied, moved and deleted with progress, cancel and conflict questions;
 the trash, drives, network places ("Connect to Server" for SFTP, SMB,
 FTP and WebDAV), thumbnails and a search by name are part of it.
 .
 In the Querencia session it opens folders (inode/directory). Bookmarks
 are shared with GTK (~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks); on its first start it
 takes over six settings of Querencia Files once.
 .
 Thumbnails of other file types than images come from the installed
 thumbnailers, which run only in a sandbox (bubblewrap, recommended).
 Network places need GVfs (gvfs-backends, recommended).
 .
 Querencia Dateien replaces Querencia Files; the package querencia-files
 now only keeps the old starters, which open Querencia Dateien.
 .
 The interface is English with a German translation (gettext); the
 translations of the shared libraries come with querencia-shell.
 .
 Querencia Desktop is developed with AI tools; every change is reviewed
 and accepted by the project owner.
 This is a beta release.
